+# GitHub-Like Dashboard Redesign Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.
+> Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Redesign the logged-in ForkMesh web app so dashboard, profile, repository, code, issue, and pull request screens closely match the supplied GitHub dark mode references while preserving existing ForkMesh data flows.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the current static dashboard architecture.
+Author source changes in dashboard partials and JS fragments, then rebuild generated assets with `tools/build_dashboard_assets.py`.
+Preserve existing data attributes and route functions wherever possible so event delegation and live mirror behavior keep working.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Cloudflare Worker static assets, Python build script, Tailwind CDN classes in authored HTML, vanilla JavaScript dashboard fragments, pytest static contract tests, browser visual verification.
+
+---
+
+## File Structure
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/shell.html` for GitHub dark design tokens, global drawer CSS, app-level responsive rules, and common utility classes.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/partials/header.html` for the GitHub-like global top bar.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/partials/sidebar.html` for the hamburger-only off-canvas navigation drawer.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/partials/main.html` for Dashboard Home, Profile Overview, Profile Repositories, Repositories, Profile Settings, Network, Chat, and Explore view containers.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/js/01-state.js` for section state, profile tab state, mock fixture helpers, and route constants if needed.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/js/04-account.js` for section routing, drawer behavior, avatar-to-settings behavior, and profile rendering hooks.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/js/05-repo-list-explorer.js` for GitHub-like repository cards, profile repository rows, sidebar top repository rows, and repository list filtering.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/js/06-repo-content.js` for tree rows, blob viewer, issues list, pull list, issue detail, pull detail, conversation cards, and diff shell styling.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/js/07-repo-compose-branch.js` for branch controls, issue composer placement, repo collection toolbar, commits, releases, insights, mirrors, and agents panel styling.
+
+Modify `public/dashboard/js/08-repo-detail-network.js` for repository header, repo tabs, code layout, About rail, route restoration, event handlers, dashboard home rendering hooks, and network rail styling.
+
+Modify tests in `tests/test_dashboard_landing_migration.py`, `tests/test_dashboard_bundle.py`, `tests/test_issue_filter_frontend.py`, and `tests/test_mirror_serving_frontend.py`.
+
+Rebuild generated `public/dashboard/index.html`, `public/dashboard.html`, and `public/dashboard.js` with `python tools/build_dashboard_assets.py`.
+
+Do not manually edit generated dashboard assets except through the build output.
+
